Correct the target from <Text>; do not copy or follow the rejected target blindly.
Paired placeholders must enclose nonblank translated text; never put a pair next to itself or around whitespace. A pair wraps the translation of the words it wraps in <Text>: never stretch it over the whole target when it wraps only part of <Text>. If a task-list marker placeholder begins <Text>, keep it first in the target.

[Example — illustration only, not this text]
<Text>: ⟦g0⟧“A⟦g1⟧bove all,” he said.
Rejected: ⟦g0⟧«Понад усе», — сказав він.
Missing: ⟦g1⟧. ⟦g0⟧…⟦g1⟧ wraps "“A" — the first letter of the first word.
Reply: {"target":"⟦g0⟧«П⟦g1⟧онад усе», — сказав він."}

Return exactly one JSON object: {"target":"<translation>"}. No code fences, no text before or after it.
